WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.560
Who can get in, and who can do anything?

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:05.330
Four gaps hand an intruder a valid badge.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:09.260
First, their breach becomes our break-in.

00:00:09.505 --> 00:00:11.875
A breached webshop leaks
a list of passwords.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.090
The same password works on our login,
and it looks like a colleague.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.650
Consider single sign-on with passkeys.

00:00:19.683 --> 00:00:22.273
Second, the second factor that is not one.

00:00:22.553 --> 00:00:25.763
Someone calls and says,
IT here, read me the code.

00:00:26.018 --> 00:00:29.308
The employee reads it out,
and the second factor is passed.

00:00:29.713 --> 00:00:31.983
Consider passkeys or hardware keys,

00:00:32.493 --> 00:00:35.263
no text message codes
and no shared logins.

00:00:36.217 --> 00:00:37.287
Third, they left.

00:00:37.632 --> 00:00:38.822
Their account did not.

00:00:39.192 --> 00:00:43.362
Six months later, four people have left,
and four accounts still work.

00:00:43.632 --> 00:00:44.882
Nobody owns them.

00:00:45.162 --> 00:00:49.112
Consider a joiner,
mover and leaver process driven by HR.

00:00:50.317 --> 00:00:52.507
Fourth, too many people can do anything.

00:00:52.807 --> 00:00:56.377
Two admins became ten,
and the last review was never.

00:00:56.652 --> 00:01:00.442
Consider just-in-time admin,
and a quarterly access review.

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:02.660
What good looks like.

00:01:02.945 --> 00:01:05.815
Identity is the perimeter now,
not the firewall.

00:01:06.205 --> 00:01:09.035
Ask how many people can do
anything in our systems.

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:12.465
And when someone last read that list,
name by name.

00:01:12.685 --> 00:01:16.795
A list longer than a page,
or an answer of not sure, is the finding.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:18.310
With personal data,

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:24.180
GDPR Article 33 requires notifying
the Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.270
within 72 hours.

00:01:28.197 --> 00:01:29.407
A suggested first step.

00:01:29.692 --> 00:01:32.322
Ask the CIO and HR for four numbers.

00:01:32.687 --> 00:01:35.357
Logins through single
sign-on with a passkey.

00:01:35.577 --> 00:01:38.327
Accounts still active a
day after the leaving date.

00:01:38.627 --> 00:01:43.057
Standing admin accounts, and rights
confirmed in the last quarterly review.

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:46.200
Identity is the perimeter.

00:01:46.605 --> 00:01:48.475
Close the doors, and read the list.

